# SurgeDPS environment template
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live service reads these from Railway → SurgeDPS service → Variables.
# Nothing in this repo auto-loads a .env file (no python-dotenv) — the local
# .env is the on-disk record of the Railway values; export vars in your
# shell (or set per-command) when running local scripts that need them.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored; NEVER commit it.

# ── Required on Railway ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Railway volume mount. Local dev falls back to <repo>/tmp_integration
# (src/persistent_paths.py).
PERSISTENT_DATA_DIR=/app/persistent

# Token gating the /__val/* debug endpoints (src/validation/private_routes.py).
# Also needed locally by scripts/seed_flood_zones_local.py and for curl-ing
# /__val/inventory.json. Value lives in the Railway dashboard.
VALIDATION_TOKEN=

# ── Optional (code defaults shown) ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Per-IP rate limit, requests/minute (scripts/api_server.py)
#SURGEDPS_RATE_LIMIT_RPM=30

# StormDPS reference API for cross-service lookups (src/reference_client.py).
# Empty disables the client. e.g. https://stormdps.com
#STORMDPS_API_URL=
#STORMDPS_API_TIMEOUT_SEC=15
#STORMDPS_REFERENCE_CACHE_MB=500

# Local IBTrACS CSV override for wind-field modeling
# (src/damage_model/wind_field.py)
#IBTRACS_CSV_PATH=

# ── Provided by Railway automatically — do not set manually ────────────────
# RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (surfaced as build_sha in /api/health), PORT

# ── Legacy AWS-era vars — NOT used by the Railway service ──────────────────
# DATA_BUCKET, CLOUDFRONT_*, HECRAS_*, PIPELINE_STATE_MACHINE_ARN, etc.
# belong to the retired AWS pipeline (src/pipeline, src/hecras, terraform/).
